<article class="env-definition" id="07N3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07N3">Definition <span data-tag="07N3">60.26.2</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/07N2" data-tag="07N2">60.26.1</a> an <em>$F$-crystal on $X/S$ (relative to $\sigma $)</em> is a pair $(\mathcal{E}, F_\mathcal {E})$ given by a crystal in finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_{X/S}$-modules $\mathcal{E}$ together with a map </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  F_\mathcal {E} : (F_ X)_{\text{cris}}^*\mathcal{E} \longrightarrow \mathcal{E}  \]
</div>
  <p> An $F$-crystal is called <em>nondegenerate</em> if there exists an integer $i \geq 0$ a map $V : \mathcal{E} \to (F_ X)_{\text{cris}}^*\mathcal{E}$ such that $V \circ F_{\mathcal{E}} = p^ i \text{id}$. </p>
</article>